# Environmental variables are loaded from these files at runtime.
# Commit only non-secret values. Secret values stay out of version control.
#
# Public, non-secret variables (safe to commit) — documented with a
# placeholder so a fresh checkout knows what to configure:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL          — the KOVA API base (with trailing path if
#                                   needed). When set, the app uses it directly.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BACKEND_URL  — the real KOVA API host (no /api suffix).
#                                   Used by the Edge middleware to rewrite the
#                                   same-origin /api fallback to the backend.
#
# How the live app connects to the API (https://kova-shopp.vercel.app):
#
#   1. If NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is set in Vercel, lib/api.ts uses it directly
#      (client + server fetches go to that host). This is the simplest, most
#      explicit setup — set it to the deployed API URL, e.g.
#        NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://kova-api.example.com/api
#
#   2. If NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is NOT set on vercel.app, lib/api.ts falls back
#      to the same-origin URL (https://kova-shopp.vercel.app/api). In that
#      case the Edge middleware (proxy.ts) rewrites /api/* to
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BACKEND_URL, so the static app and the API can live on
#      different hosts while the browser sees a single origin.
#
#   3. Local dev always uses NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001 from
#      .env.local, so the middleware rewrite is never involved locally.
#
# Pick ONE approach for production:
#   • Approach A (recommended, simplest): set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL in Vercel
#     to the deployed API URL. Leave NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BACKEND_URL empty.
#   • Approach B (same-origin): leave NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL empty in Vercel and
#     set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BACKEND_URL to the deployed API host (no /api
#     suffix). proxy.ts rewrites /api/* to that host.
#
# Secret values that should NEVER be committed (kept in .env.local or Vercel):
#   CLERK_SECRET_KEY
#   CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY  (public, but kept out of the repo by convention)
#   DATABASE_URL           (frontend does not use this — it belongs in kova-api)
#   PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY    (backend only)
#   RESEND_API_KEY         (backend only)
#   CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET  (backend only)

# Public API base URL — set this in Vercel when using Approach A.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=""

# Real API host (no /api suffix) — set this in Vercel when using Approach B
# (same-origin /api rewrite). Leave empty when using Approach A.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BACKEND_URL=""
